    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0899" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg837"/>

                <head>No. 495.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 18, 1878</date>.
                        (Received May 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 70.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 24, and
                    to my dispatches Nos. 62, 64, and 67, I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    copy and translation of a note which I have this day received from the President
                    of the confederation.</p>
                <p>As stated in my No. 68, the Federal Council has decided to take part in the
                    proposed conference under section 2 of the act of February 28 last.</p>
                <p>I respectfully ask that a copy of the act may be furnished me for the files of
                    the legation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp; c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>NICHOLAS FISH.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d500-a1.xml" xpointer="d500-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
